===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*preyH-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|frend}}, {{m|enm|freend}}, from {{inh|en|ang|frēond||friend|lit=loving[-one], lover}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*friund}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*frijōndz||lover, friend}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*preyH-||to like, love}}, equivalent to {{suffix|enm|free|and|alt2=nd}}.

Cognate with {{cog|stq|Fjund}}, {{m|stq|Früünd|t=friend}}, {{cog|fy|freon}}, {{m|fy|froen}}, {{m|fy|freondinne||friend}}, {{cog|nl|vriend||friend}}, {{cog|nds|Frund}}, {{m|nds|Fründ||friend, relative}}, {{cog|lb|Frënd|t=friend}}, {{cog|de|Freund||friend}}, {{cog|da|frænde||kinsman}}, {{cog|sv|frände||kinsman, relative}}, {{cog|is|frændi||kinsman}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐍂𐌹𐌾𐍉𐌽𐌳𐍃||friend}}. More at {{m|en|free}}.

Other cognates include {{cog|ru|приятель||friend}} and {{cog|sa|प्रिय|tr=priyá-||beloved}}.

